          <div class="w2-service-detail">
            <p class="w2-service-overline">01 <span>Concrete &amp; foundation</span></p>
            <h3 id="w2-service-title-slab">Slab leak detection</h3>
            <p class="w2-service-description">Slab leaks occur in water lines routed through or beneath a concrete foundation. Because the pipe is concealed, clues may appear somewhere else: a warm or damp floor, a water meter that moves while fixtures are off, the sound of running water, or an unexplained increase in water use. A detection visit starts by documenting where symptoms appear and which plumbing lines may run beneath the floor. The technician evaluates those clues and uses appropriate checks to narrow the likely source and affected area without opening the concrete as part of the locating process. You receive an explanation of the findings and the location indicated by the inspection, giving you useful information to discuss next steps with the service provider of your choice.</p>
            <div class="w2-service-clues"><span>Warm flooring</span><span>Unexplained water use</span><span>Sound below the floor</span></div>
            <a class="w2-service-action" href="#contact">Request slab leak detection <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
