            <p class="w2-service-overline">05 <span>Drainage &amp; waste lines</span></p>
            <h3 id="w2-service-title-drain">Drain &amp; sewer leak detection</h3>
            <p class="w2-service-description">Drain and sewer piping carries wastewater away from a property, so a leak may appear as recurring wet soil, an unpleasant odor, dampness near a cleanout, or changes around a floor drain. These signs can have other causes, and a drain concern is investigated differently from a pressurized water-supply leak. An assessment starts with the location and timing of the issue, the fixtures involved, and visible symptoms. The pipe layout and available access help guide the investigation and determine whether the evidence points toward a drain or sewer line. We explain what was observed, which areas were checked, and whether additional evaluation by another qualified provider may be appropriate. This service locates and documents suspected leaks; it does not include drain or sewer repairs.</p>
            <div class="w2-service-clues"><span>Recurring damp area</span><span>Drain odors</span><span>Floor drain changes</span></div>
            <a class="w2-service-action" href="#contact">Request drain &amp; sewer detection <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>

